# Line endings, enforced -- this repo is edited on Windows and RUN inside WSL.
#
# A shell script with CRLF endings fails in bash in a way that reads as nonsense: session 6 lost
# a training run to `cd: $'/home/sleem/bringwrench\r': No such file or directory` after a
# Windows-side edit rewrote ops/train_vla.sh with \r\n. core.autocrlf would reintroduce it on
# every checkout, so the eol is pinned per type instead of left to the client's config.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf

# Windows-side launchers, which cmd.exe and PowerShell expect to be CRLF.
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

*.mp4       binary
*.png       binary
*.npz       binary
